{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And they made the tunics of fine linen</b> etc. <b>and the turban of fine linen, and the ornamental caps of fine linen, and the linen breeches of fine twined linen.</b> In these two verses there are five occurrences of שש together with הבד, which is also שש — one for its own meaning, and the rest for derash. This is what they derived in tractate Yoma, chapter Ba Lo, on these two verses, saying: 'Five verses are written' — meaning, two verses in which שש occurs five times, and it would have sufficed to write one of them at the end. One is for its own meaning, as it is a matter of derash — for since it is written elsewhere ״כתנת בד״ and here it is written ״את הכתנות שש״, this indicates that the שש is linen (בד), as they said there: בד — that which grows from the ground, בד in בד, and that is flax; שש — that its threads should be sixfold; שש — that they should be twisted; שש — for things in which שש is not stated, such as the me'il; שש לעכובא — meaning, lest you say it is merely for a mitzvah but does not disqualify if omitted, therefore it was further necessary to add שש לעכובא. And what is written in the third verse, ״ואת האבנט שש משזר״, was not needed for its own meaning, since בד is already stated regarding the avnet; rather, it was needed for the other types of avnet, to require that each of them be שש."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:55.630099357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}